    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is well-placed overall: a dedicated `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning` function sits alongside its siblings (`FlagOwnerBulkSignup`, `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate`), the pipeline wiring/governance matches the neighbours, and the model field + 4-dialect schema + openapi additions are complete and consistent. But there is one structural issue worth fixing.\n\n**Finding: the \"count owners in a city\" logic is duplicated across the hard-reject and the soft-warning, against this codebase's own established pattern.**\n\n- `CheckOwnerCityCapacity.service` (lines 23\u201325) and the new `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning.service` both inline the identical query: `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(... city.equals(existing.getCity())).count()`. The new class's own Javadoc admits this (\"This mirrors the count used by `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\"). Two copies of the same per-city count means the hard limit (50) and the warning band (40\u201349) can silently drift apart.\n- The codebase already shows the preferred shape for exactly this situation: `FlagOwnerBulkSignup` and the daily-limit check do **not** re-implement the per-day count \u2014 they share `BusinessDays.createdOn(...)`. The city case should follow suit: extract a shared helper (e.g. `OwnerCities.countInCity(ownerRepository, city)` or a repository method) and have both `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` and `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning` call it. Without this, `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning` is quietly re-deriving a rule that lives elsewhere.\n- Symptom of the drift already present: `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` uses `city.equals(existing.getCity())` (no null guard) while `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning` adds `city != null && city.equals(...)`. The two \"same\" counts have already diverged in null-handling \u2014 a single shared helper would settle this in one place.\n- `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` is now a private constant in two classes. If the shared helper doesn't own it, at minimum the two steps that key off the same limit should not each define their own copy.\n\nSuggested shape: one helper returning the owners-in-city count; `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` rejects at `>= CITY_CAPACITY`, `FlagOwnerCapacityWarning` flags at `>= WARNING_THRESHOLD && < CITY_CAPACITY`, both over the same count definition.",
